From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] tcp-bbr3: add adaptive LFN loss tolerance and fix listener lifecycle safety

Adaptive loss tolerance for long-fat network (LFN) and cross-carrier paths,
specifically for OpenWrt default fq_codel (target 5ms, interval 100ms):
- Round-based loss accounting:
  bbr_lfn_round_measured() strictly separates zero loss from small sample rounds.
- Cruise phase floor learning:
  Learns physical loss floor up to cap only during cruise rounds with
  min_qd <= 2ms, rate <= cap, and flight reaching at least 0.50x BDP to avoid
  starved proxy rounds clearing slope_bad. Requires 4 consecutive clean rounds.
- Probe phase slope protection:
  Tracks probing status directly in bbr_lfn_note_sample() before phase
  transitions can overwrite cycle_idx on loss ACKs.
  Trips lfn_slope_bad if probe loss exceeds cruise floor by >= 1%.
- 5ms fq_codel hard cutoff:
  Rounds with min_qd > 5ms immediately deny loss tolerance and reset cruise rounds.
- Starlink / burst queue drop recovery:
  lfn_cut_by_queue set only when inflight_hi cut by queue > 5ms. Restored to
  1.0x BDP on subsequent round when min_qd <= 2ms and rate <= floor.
- Fast-path micro-optimizations:
  Check cached min_rtt < 20ms before querying netns sysctls to avoid pointer
  indirection on LAN/WiFi. Inline round-start check on round finish exit.
- Listening socket lifecycle safety and retry on allocation failure:
  Do not allocate struct bbr for TCP_CLOSE or TCP_LISTEN sockets. Cloned child
  sockets inherit NULL and allocate their own block on first transmission.
  If allocation fails under memory pressure, slot remains NULL and retries
  on subsequent ACKs.

Signed-off-by: QiuSimons <45143996+QiuSimons@users.noreply.github.com>
